# .gitleaksignore - audited baseline of pre-existing findings
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Until #630 this repo's .gitleaks.toml declared an [allowlist] but no [[rules]]
# and no [extend] block. gitleaks therefore loaded ZERO rules and detected
# nothing: every nightly full-history scan was green because secret scanning was
# effectively switched off. #630 added "[extend] useDefault = true", enabling the
# default ruleset for the first time. That surfaced 823 accumulated historical
# findings at once and turned the nightly scan plus every PR's Tier-1
# system-audit red.
#
# ~757 of those were generated or vendored corpora (sprint-audit JSON reports,
# attestation file-hash maps, the vendored Sonar rule corpus) and are handled by
# path entries in .gitleaks.toml. The 66 fingerprints below are the audited
# remainder.
#
# WHAT WAS VERIFIED (2026-07-25)
# Every one of the 66 was decoded and classified before being baselined:
#   - 18 JWTs issued by the real Supabase project ref, role=authenticated,
#     captured into k6 benchmark artifacts by load-test runs.
#     ALL EXPIRED (latest exp 2026-02-28).
#   -  3 Supabase local-dev demo anon keys (iss=supabase-demo; public, documented)
#   -  4 canonical jwt.io sample tokens (sub=1234567890)
#   -  6 Stripe test-mode literals (sk/pk/pi test-prefixed placeholders with
#     sequential or obviously-fake bodies; not reproduced here because Trivy's
#     secret scanner flags the literal form even inside a comment)
#   - remainder: sequential/synthetic fixtures (ifc_live_ + sequential hex),
#     UUIDs, SHA-256 attestation hashes, a base32 TOTP test seed,
#     and SonarQube's default admin:admin in local monitoring compose config.
# No live credential was found. No rotation was required.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT PATH-ALLOWLISTED
# artifacts/benchmarks/ is baselined by fingerprint, NOT added to the
# .gitleaks.toml path allowlist. Future k6 runs mint NEW tokens with NEW
# fingerprints, so they will still be caught. A path allowlist there would
# silently swallow them - the same fake-green failure mode this file documents.
#
# SOURCE NOW FIXED (#643): k6 summary handlers redact tokens before writing
# (tools/scripts/k6/lib/redact.js strips setup_data + JWT-shaped strings), so no
# NEW token fingerprints will accrue here. The 18 historical fingerprints below
# STAY: they pin immutable historical commits scanned by the nightly full-history
# job; dropping them would red that scan (no history rewrite is performed, and
# all 18 are expired — no rotation required).
#
# MAINTENANCE
# Do not append to this file to make a scan pass. A new fingerprint means a new
# secret reached history: triage it, rotate if real, then regenerate this
# baseline deliberately.


